{
 "ep": 11,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "PostgreSQL Configuration Files",
 "phase": "Foundations",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Three PostgreSQL config files you must understand.",
   "cap": "Three *PostgreSQL* *config* files you must understand."
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode eleven of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: the config files, and how to check them safely.",
   "cap": "Episode 11: the *config* *files,* checked *safely.*",
   "cue": "safely"
  },
  {
   "say": "PostgreSQL has three hand-edited config files. By default, all three live in the data directory.",
   "cap": "Three hand-edited files. Default home: the *data* *directory.*",
   "cue": "data"
  },
  {
   "say": "postgresql.conf holds server settings: memory, logging, connections and more.",
   "cap": "*postgresql.conf:* the server *settings.*",
   "cue": "settings"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_hba.conf decides who may connect. H B A means host-based authentication.",
   "cap": "*pg_hba.conf:* who may *connect.*",
   "cue": "host-based"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_ident.conf maps operating system users to database users, for methods like peer.",
   "cap": "*pg_ident.conf:* OS user to *database* *user.*",
   "cue": "peer"
  },
  {
   "say": "Step one: don't guess where they are. Ask the server: SHOW config_file and SHOW hba_file.",
   "cap": "Ask the server: *SHOW* *config_file.*",
   "cue": "SHOW"
  },
  {
   "say": "On this Ubuntu package, the files sit under slash etc, not in the data directory. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "Ubuntu package: config in */etc,* data in */var/lib.*",
   "cue": "Output"
  },
  {
   "say": "The format is simple: one setting per line, name equals value, and a hash starts a comment.",
   "cap": "One *setting* per line. *#* starts a comment.",
   "cue": "hash"
  },
  {
   "say": "If the same setting appears twice, only the last one counts.",
   "cap": "Same setting twice? The *last* one *wins.*",
   "cue": "last"
  },
  {
   "say": "include_dir pulls in every dot conf file in a folder, in name order.",
   "cap": "*include_dir* reads *.conf* files in name order.",
   "cue": "order"
  },
  {
   "say": "ALTER SYSTEM writes postgresql.auto.conf, which overrides postgresql.conf. Don't edit it by hand.",
   "cap": "*ALTER SYSTEM* writes *postgresql.auto.conf.*",
   "cue": "overrides"
  },
  {
   "say": "Most changes need only a reload: pg_ctl reload, or SELECT pg_reload_conf.",
   "cap": "Apply with a *reload:* *pg_reload_conf().*",
   "cue": "reload"
  },
  {
   "say": "Some, like shared_buffers, need a restart. pg_settings then shows pending_restart true.",
   "cap": "*shared_buffers* needs a *restart.*",
   "cue": "pending_restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Safe inspection: pg_file_settings shows every entry in the files, and whether it could be applied.",
   "cap": "*pg_file_settings:* was each entry *applied?*",
   "cue": "applied"
  },
  {
   "say": "The first row is false because a later entry overrides it. The second needs a restart.",
   "cap": "Overridden or *needs* *restart:* both show *f.*",
   "cue": "second"
  },
  {
   "say": "Now pg_hba.conf. Each rule has a type, database, user, address and auth method.",
   "cap": "Each rule: *type,* *database,* *user,* *address,* *method.*",
   "cue": "method"
  },
  {
   "say": "Rules are checked top to bottom, and the first match wins. If that login fails, no later rule is tried.",
   "cap": "*First* *match* wins. *No* fall-through.",
   "cue": "first"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_hba_file_rules shows the rules exactly as the server parsed them.",
   "cap": "*pg_hba_file_rules:* the parsed rules.",
   "cue": "parsed"
  },
  {
   "say": "Common mistake: a typo, like trusst. The view shows the error before you reload.",
   "cap": "A typo shows up in the *error* column.",
   "cue": "error"
  },
  {
   "say": "Reload anyway, and the log says pg_hba.conf was not reloaded. Old rules stay.",
   "cap": "Bad file? *Not* *reloaded.* Old rules *stay.*",
   "cue": "log"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway: a common practice is to back up the file, edit, check these views, then reload.",
   "cap": "Back up, edit, *check* the views, then *reload.*",
   "cue": "check"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: postgresql.conf holds settings. pg_hba.conf controls access.",
   "cap": "Recap: *settings* and *access.*",
   "cue": "access"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_ident.conf maps names. Last entry wins, first match wins.",
   "cap": "*Name* *maps.* *Last* entry, *first* match.",
   "cue": "Last"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: PostgreSQL versions and release types. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *versions* and releases. *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
